<summary>How to read the portfolio</summary>
<p>Four value layers: premium identity rights (Emirates, Deel sleeve), fan distribution and experiences (WhatsApp, Facebook, Oakley Meta), matchday consumption (Guinness, Coca-Cola) and operational capability (Airwallex, Deel HR). This is an analyst classification and a partner may serve more than one layer. Without contracts it would be misleading to count Meta, WhatsApp, Facebook and Oakley Meta as four independent economic wins. No reviewed release provides independently verified sales lift, customer acquisition cost or partner ROI. <a href="#P1">[P1-P11]</a></p>
<p>Negotiating-leverage hypothesis: stronger revenue, recent sporting results and a broad global identity could improve Arsenal&#x27;s bargaining position. The Emirates renewal fits that reading but reveals nothing about competing bids or bonus clauses. <a href="#P1">[P1, </a><a href="#P2">P2, </a><a href="#F4">F4, </a><a href="#F8">F8]</a></p>
</details>
</section>

